# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Obsidian vault and editor state — NEVER auto-commit these.
#
# `Quant Brain/` is a 255,897-file / 4.2 GB imported research vault containing a
# THIRD PARTY's project (github.com/DonovanWillis/QuantModel, authored on macOS
# under /Users/donov/) plus agent-orchestration payloads. It has been swept into
# this repository twice by unattended `git add -A`:
#   592e11a "dcfhtg"  2026-09-13 19:50  3,199 files / 1,674,621 insertions
#   bb4bbf8 "igkhghk" 2026-09-13 21:31  3,200 files / 1,675,180 insertions
# Both were unpushed and were reverted; recovery refs
# `accidental-vault-commit-592e11a` and `accidental-vault-commit-bb4bbf8` retain
# them. Neither contained a credential (verified: 0 secret-shaped additions).
#
# It also carries `Quant Brain/.codex/config.toml` with approval_policy="never"
# and sandbox_mode="danger-full-access", whose own header says it must not be
# committed, and `Quant Brain/.claude/helpers/auto-commit.sh`, which runs
# `git add -A` and pushes with AUTO_PUSH defaulting to true against THIS repo's
# public origin.
#
# Versioning the vault is a deliberate architectural decision, not an accident.
# If that decision is ever taken, commit explicitly with `git add -f` after
# removing the executable agent payloads. Until then it stays on disk, untracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Quant Brain/
.obsidian/
